+# RTGL1 with VK_KHR_ray_query (Android port, part 1)
+
+Branch `ray-query-android`, based on **v1.1.1**, the version PrBoom+ RT
+(`sultim-t/prboom-plus-rt`, April 2022) was built against.
+
+The renderer no longer needs `VK_KHR_ray_tracing_pipeline`, which most
+Android GPUs don't expose. It needs:
+
+- `VK_KHR_ray_query`, `VK_KHR_acceleration_structure`, `VK_KHR_deferred_host_operations`
+- `VK_KHR_synchronization2`, Vulkan 1.2
+- features: `rayQuery`, `accelerationStructure`, `bufferDeviceAddress`,
+  `runtimeDescriptorArray`, `shaderSampledImageArrayNonUniformIndexing`,
+  `shaderFloat16`, `shaderInt16`, `multiview`, `samplerAnisotropy`,
+  `shaderStorageImageExtendedFormats`
+
+Other features are enabled only if present. Missing requirements and too-low
+descriptor limits fail at startup with a message naming them.
+
+## What changed
+
+| Commit | Change |
+|---|---|
+| Shaders: getTexture macro | builds with current glslang |
+| Portability | unified-memory fallback (phones have no host-visible non-device-local memory), optional validation layers / debug utils, VMA include |
+| Ray query | 4 raygen shaders -> compute shaders tracing with `rayQueryEXT`; closest-hit, miss and any-hit (alpha test) inlined; barriers and descriptor stages moved from ray tracing to compute; device selection and features for ray query |
+| 4 descriptor sets | path tracer bound 9 sets; Adreno 7xx allows 8 (older GPUs 4). Small sets are copied into one each frame |
+| Limit check | descriptor, workgroup and push constant limits checked at startup |
+
+## Verification (lavapipe, Mesa 25.2, software Vulkan)
+
+A test scene with alpha-tested, mirror and glass geometry, a sun, a sphere
+light and a dynamic object, rendered for 60 frames at 637x357 (not a multiple
+of the 8x8 workgroup):
+
+- output is **pixel-identical** to the original ray tracing pipeline build
+- a deliberately broken alpha test changes 6.5% of pixels, so the comparison detects real errors
+- no new validation messages; the descriptor set limit error is gone
+- all 42 shaders pass `spirv-val`
+
+Not verified: real Android hardware. Speed, driver bugs and format support
+can only be checked on the device.
+
+## Building
+
+Desktop (Linux):
+
+```
+cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo -DRG_WITH_SURFACE_XLIB=ON
+cmake --build build
+mkdir -p Build && cd Source/Shaders && python3 GenerateShaders.py   # -> Build/*.spv
+```
+
+## Remaining work for Android
+
+1. **Surface**: add `VK_KHR_android_surface` (an `RgAndroidSurfaceCreateInfo`
+   taking an `ANativeWindow*`, like the existing Xlib/Win32 ones).
+2. **Build**: NDK toolchain (`-DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=$NDK/build/cmake/android.toolchain.cmake -DANDROID_ABI=arm64-v8a -DANDROID_PLATFORM=android-30`);
+   link `libvulkan.so` from the NDK. Package `Build/*.spv`, the blue noise and
+   water normal `.ktx2` files as assets and load them through `RgInstanceCreateInfo::pfnOpenFile` /
+   `pfnCloseFile` (e.g. with `AAssetManager`), as Android assets are not
+   plain files.
+3. **PrBoom+ RT**: SDL2 Android project, touch controls, WAD location, and
+   passing the window to RTGL1.
+4. **On-device checks**: the B10G11R11 framebuffer is a blit destination with
+   linear upscaling (lavapipe lacks that format feature); run with the
+   validation layer packaged once to catch device-specific issues.
+5. **Performance**: start at a low render resolution with FSR upscaling.
